<%= render layout: "shared/legal", locals: { heading: "Refunds & Returns" } do %>
  <p>
    Every item is printed to order with the artwork chosen for it, so it cannot be resold. That shapes
    the policy below. Nothing here removes the statutory rights you have where you live — including
    rights covering faulty goods, which apply whether or not an item was made to order.
  </p>

  <h2>Faulty, damaged or wrong items</h2>
  <p>
    If an item arrives damaged, misprinted, or is not what you ordered,
    <%= link_to "contact us", contact_path %> within <strong>30 days of delivery</strong> with your order
    number and photos of the item and the packaging. We will reprint it or refund it in full, whichever you prefer.
    You will not normally need to send the item back.
  </p>

  <h2>Change of mind</h2>
  <p>
    Because items are personalised and made to order, we cannot accept returns simply because you changed
    your mind, and the usual right to cancel a distance sale does not apply to custom-made goods. If you
    contact us before production begins we will do our best to cancel or amend the order.
  </p>

  <h2>Cancelling an order</h2>
  <p>
    Orders usually go into production shortly after payment. Email us as soon as possible with your order
    number: if production has not started we cancel and refund in full; if it has, we cannot cancel.
  </p>

  <h2>Wrong or incomplete delivery address</h2>
  <p>
    If a parcel is returned to us because the address was wrong or incomplete, we will reship it once the
    correct address is confirmed, at the cost of reshipment. Please check the address carefully at
    checkout.
  </p>

  <h2>Lost parcels</h2>
  <p>
    If tracking shows no movement, or a parcel is confirmed lost in transit, contact us and we will
    reprint or refund the order. For unrecovered parcels marked delivered, we will investigate with the
    carrier before deciding.
  </p>

  <h2>Orders we cannot produce</h2>
  <p>
    If an order fails in production, is cancelled by our print partner, or is returned as undeliverable,
    we refund the full amount automatically to the original payment method and email you to explain.
  </p>

  <h2>How refunds are paid</h2>
  <p>
    Refunds go back to the original payment method through Stripe. We process them as soon as the outcome
    is agreed; how quickly the money appears is up to your bank, typically within 5 to 10 business days.
    Shipping costs are refunded when the fault is ours.
  </p>

  <h2>Chargebacks</h2>
  <p>
    Please contact us before raising a chargeback with your bank — it is almost always faster to resolve
    directly. Where an order is refunded or charged back, any developer commission on that sale is
    reversed.
  </p>

  <h2>For developers</h2>
  <p>
    Refunds triggered by production failures are automatic and do not count against your account. If your
    users report a recurring print quality problem, tell us with order numbers and photos so we can raise
    it with our print partner.
  </p>
<% end %>
